2022 was supposed to be different after  a record-breaking year of home price  appreciation last year the housing  market was supposed to cool down  i even made a video about it  well it hasn't happened yet in fact home  prices this year are setting brand new  record highs i want to tell you why the  housing market has been so hot to start  this year defying real estate economist  predictions explain what we're seeing in  the market that suggests housing prices  really are starting to cool in detail  how home prices will affect inflation  and the economy moving forward  let's get into it  economists laid out some keys to a  cooler market in 2022 after 2021's  scalding hot year one of them was an  increase in the supply of available  housing and we've seen that  sort of the monthly supply of new homes  on the market in april was the highest  in 12 years  unfortunately new homes are a small part  of the overall housing market and at the  sales pace we saw in april there was  just a two month supply of houses  available for sale and even though  mortgage rates jumped from 3.8 at the  beginning of march to 5.3 percent in  mid-may there were still enough buyers  and not enough houses  so prices kept going up finally  inflation has remained elevated so far  this year with supply chain issues and  worker shortages continuing to drive up  prices  but things are starting to change and  we're seeing signs of a slowdown in the  housing market in may realtor.com noted  the first year-over-year increase in  overall housing supply since june 2019  the increase in housing supply has come  largely as a result of weakening sales  finally catching up to the market sales  of existing homes have been lower year  over year every month since august 2021  pending home sales have declined for six  consecutive months and are at the  slowest pace in nearly a decade higher  mortgage rates and average home prices  well above 350 000  have also taken millions of potential  buyers out of the market according to  the national association of realtors  more homes on the market plus less  eligible buyers  usually means prices go down and we're  starting to see that almost one in five  u.s home sellers lowered their asking  price in may the highest number since  october 2019. mark zandi chief economist  at moody's analytics tells me home  prices face a meaningful comeuppance  he's expecting them to go flat by the  end of this year or early next year with  price declines in a significant number  of markets  this slowdown is likely a good thing for  the economy because housing prices are a  major contributor to inflation with home  prices jumping at double-digit rates  economists predict rent inflation will  rise by almost twice the pre-pandemic  five-year average this year  and next year housing prices also make  up a major part of the core inflation  readings that the federal reserve  watches to check the economy's  temperature a sustained slowdown in  housing prices could mean the fed  doesn't have to raise interest rates as  high or for as long which could help the  u.s avoid a recession and we've seen  over the past year that higher home  prices aren't having their typical  impact of boosting consumer sentiment as  home prices have spiked to record highs  consumer sentiment has declined falling  to decade lows in recent months  back in the day the great talib quali  told us what the good life could be he  said let's toast to paid mortgages  lasting marriages tina ferris is king to  paris  living long making my kids heirs and  heiresses  that's all for now see you next time  [Music]
 

